---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How CalcYourFinance handles your data: our calculators run in your browser, we don't store your inputs, and we explain exactly what analytics and ads collect."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <section class="container mx-auto max-w-[52rem] px-4 py-6 pb-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy Policy" }]} />
    <h1 class="my-5">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Last updated: {SITE.effectiveDate}.</p>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} ("we", "us") operates {SITE.domain}. This policy explains what
        information we collect and how we use it. In short: our calculators run
        entirely in your browser, and we do not collect or store the numbers you type
        into them.
      </p>

      <h2>Calculator inputs</h2>
      <p>
        Every calculation on this site happens locally in your browser using
        client-side JavaScript. The amounts, prices and other values you enter are
        <strong>not sent to our servers and are not stored or logged by us</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some calculators keep a short list of your recent calculations so you can
        return to one. That list is written to your own browser's local storage, on
        your device only — it is never uploaded to us and we cannot read it. You can
        remove it with the "Clear" control on the calculator, or by clearing site data
        in your browser. Values you enter anywhere else are discarded when you close
        or reload the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics to understand aggregate usage — for example which
        calculators are popular and which countries visitors come from. It sets
        cookies or similar identifiers and collects data such as your approximate
        location, device type, browser and the pages you view. It does
        <strong>not</strong> receive the values you enter into calculators. Google's
        use of that data is governed by its own privacy policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        We may display advertising from third-party networks (such as Google AdSense)
        to support the free tools. Ad partners may use cookies to serve and measure
        ads. You can control ad personalisation through your browser settings and
        through the ad provider's own settings. When advertising is enabled, this
        section will reflect the specific partners in use.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Our own use is limited to your browser's local storage, which stays on your
        device: your light or dark theme preference, and the recent-calculations list
        described above. Analytics and, if enabled, advertising partners may set their
        own cookies as described above. You can clear or block cookies and site data in
        your browser at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Because we don't collect personal accounts or store your inputs, there is no
        profile to delete. You can disable cookies, use your browser's "do not track"
        and ad-personalisation controls, or contact us with any privacy question.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This site is intended for a general, adult audience and is not directed at children.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site evolves. Material changes will be
        reflected by the "last updated" date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> or see our
        <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
